From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 16:39:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 16/46] fix(prompts): stop role templates restating formula
 commands lossily (gcp-co9)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A refinery rejection orphaned a bead: the refinery role prompt's condensed
"Rejection Flow" restated mol-refinery-patrol's pool-return `gc bd update`
without `--set-metadata gc.routed_to=...`, and the prompt is what is injected at
spawn while the formula must be opened deliberately. Nothing spawns for a bead
with no routing, so it sat open and unassigned indefinitely while the refinery
reported a successful rejection. The state is indistinguishable from a healthy
pooled bead, and witness patrols are correctly told not to flag unassigned pool
beads — so the one observer positioned to catch it is instructed to ignore it.

Patching that one flag would have left the drift class intact: two sources of
truth for the same command, where the lossy copy is the injected one. This
audits every restated formula command across gastown/agents/*/ and resolves each
by pointing at the owning formula step instead of copying it — a pointer cannot
drift, a copy can. Six lossy restatements were found and fixed:

- refinery Rejection Flow dropped `gc.routed_to` and the `gc workflow
  delete-source/reopen-source` cleanup. This one keeps a verbatim copy of the
  routing update, explicitly marked as a copy naming the authoritative steps
  (`rebase`, `handle-failures`), because the acceptance bar is that the injected
  prompt alone yields a routed bead.
- refinery Patrol Lifecycle Rules 1 and 2 each restated next-iteration's
  pour/burn without the `gc runtime drain-ack` that precedes every formula
  bail-out; a session that exits 1 without acking is never recycled.
- deacon and witness "No Idle State" fallbacks had the same missing ack.
- witness and deacon warrant blocks (and their quick-reference rows) dropped the
  open-warrant dedup guard every formula copy carries; a duplicate warrant races
  a second shutdown dance against the same target.

Two inline commands are kept because there is nothing to point at, and both are
now complete rather than condensed: boot has no formula, so its warrant command
gains the dedup guard; the polecat claim block's CLAIM_RELEASED path now sets
`gc.routed_to` when it returns an unreadable bead to the pool — it can release
directly-assigned work that never carried pool routing, which is the same
silent-orphan shape. Cold-start wisp pours are marked bootstrap-only with a
pointer to the step that owns every later pour.

tests/test_prompt_formula_command_drift.py locks in the three invariants whose
loss was observed, so the next formula edit cannot silently re-diverge:
pool-returning updates declare routing, warrant creation in injected context is
deduped, prompt bail-out paths drain-ack. Written red first — it reported
exactly the 12 sites found by hand — then green. gastown/README.md documents the
convention and its three exceptions.

Rebased onto integration 41ccd40 after the original branch was held. Five
conflicted hunks, each resolved by verifying that the pointer target really
carries what the inline copy gained since the fork at e82ecfb — a pointer that
lands on a staler command silently reverts the fix that was made inline:

- refinery Rules 1 and 2, and the witness fallback, gained `--include-infra`
  from dabcb2c (gcp-xbl). mol-refinery-patrol.toml and mol-witness-patrol.toml
  both already carry it, so those pointers are safe as written.
- The witness warrant pointer lands on mol-witness-patrol `check-polecat-health`
  step 3, which files the warrant deduped and with `gc.routed_to`. Safe.
- The deacon fallback was NOT safe. dabcb2c gave the deacon prompt the
  surplus-wisp reconcile the witness already had, but landed it only in the
  prompt; mol-deacon-patrol's `next-iteration` still poured unconditionally.
  Pointing at it as-shipped would have dropped the reconcile. So the claim above
  no longer holds for one formula: mol-deacon-patrol.toml section 3 now carries
  the reconcile, modelled on mol-witness-patrol's, keeping the formula's own
  fail-closed drain-ack on each bail-out. Effective behaviour is unchanged — the
  deacon runs whichever copy it reads, and both now reconcile.
- gastown/README.md conflicted only because the new section landed where the
  approval-gate section (gcp-a22/amo/dc8) had since been inserted. Both are kept.

The other formulas are unchanged; they were already correct.

Validation: go vet/build/test clean; validate_registry.py ok; the three gastown
shell suites pass; the full CI pytest set passes in a clean environment. Seven
failures appear when the suite is run from inside a gastown agent session — they
reproduce identically on the clean base and are env leakage (GC_BIN, GC_TEMPLATE)
filed as gcp-9ur, discovered-from this bead.

Downstream: these templates reach running agents via pack pin + redeploy, so no
live agent picks up the fix until the pack is redeployed.
